  "notes": "Measured 2026-11-23 on N940N (DC-9-32, left side, 1984) and drawn on the MD-82 (Republic flew both in it); the MD-82 photo shows the same layout. Heights converted from projected to girth shares. Republic never had an ICAO code (it closed in 1986), so it's keyed RC1979. For Skyarium's ghost flights. The Convair 580's paint (types.CVLT) is measured on N968N, 1982.",
  "types": {
    "CVLT": {
      "note": "On the Convair 580 (N968N, Atlanta 1982, sourceRefs 2; measured on shapes/CVLT.json with tools/photo_trace.py's fit and along the body by the nose, the flight deck's aft pane, three windows behind the wing and the tail cone): the bands run straight along the body with a navy pinstripe on the upper band's top edge; the nose's point starts 1.4 m back and its diagonal meets the upper band 5.6 m back, ahead of the propeller; the windows' white strip ends forward in a slanted square end 4-5.5 m back. The title, behind the propeller and over the wing's root, is lower than on the DC-9, its letters reaching below the upper band. The nose is white (no dark radome), the nacelles bare metal. The fin's trailing-edge band is a broad light blue to the trailing edge with a thin navy line along its forward edge, and Herman sits low and forward on the tall fin. Heights are good to about 0.05 of the side (the photo looks up from a few degrees below), positions along the body to about 0.2 m. The 1979-80 photos (sourceRefs 3) show the interim North Central look, not this.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "sourceRefs": [
        2
      ],
